        "scope": "in_scope",
        "statement": "For every $n,d\\geq3$, define\n\\[\n T=d^2-3d+3,\\quad\n w_*=-\\frac{2d-3}{dT},\\quad\n p_* =\\frac{(d-2)^2}{Tk},\\quad\n e_* =\\frac1{(d-1)^3+1},\\quad\n h=\\frac1{d^2(d-2)},\n\\]\nwith $k$ as in \\eqref{eq:rank}. Then $0<p_*<1$, $w(p_*)=w_*$, and\n\\begin{equation}\n \\eps^{n,d}(p_*)=e_* < e_*+h p_*\\left(1-\\frac RM\\right)\n                  \\leq \\EG(\\rho(p_*)).\n\\end{equation}\nIn particular, for $n=d=3$ one has $p_*=3/8$ and\n\\begin{equation}\n \\eps^{3,3}(3/8)=\\frac19=\\frac{12}{108}\n       <\\frac{13}{108}\\leq\\EG(\\rho_{3,3}(3/8)).\n\\end{equation}",
        "status": "preparing",
